Package: codyn
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip
Recommends: python3.10, rsync, perl
Suggests: gromacs, openbabel
Maintainer: Moisés Maia <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian/CODYN
Description: Computational platform for protein-ligand molecular dynamics (GROMACS)
 CODYN is a PyQt5-based graphical tool that automates protein-multiligand
 molecular dynamics with GROMACS: ligand parametrization (CHARMM36/CGenFF
 or AMBER/GAFF), complex assembly, solvation and ionization, energy
 minimization, NVT/NPT equilibration, production runs, MM/PBSA and MM/GBSA
 with gmx_MMPBSA, and trajectory analysis (RMSD, RMSF, SASA, H-bonds,
 radius of gyration).
 .
 This package installs the application files to /opt/codyn and a menu
 launcher. On first run, CODYN itself creates an isolated Python virtual
 environment at ~/.venv/CODYN. GROMACS, CUDA and gmx_MMPBSA are installed on
 demand from the "Install requirements" window — this package does not
 install them as root during installation, by design (see
 packaging/deb/README.md).
